cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RegisterAlgebra: reference implementation of exact register arithmetic"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kalendar
    given-names: Ruslan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3986-2460"
    affiliation: "Helsinki Institute of Life Science (HiLIFE), University of Helsinki"
    email: ruslan.kalendar@helsinki.fi
repository-code: "https://github.com/rkalendar/RegisterAlgebra"
abstract: >-
  Pure-Python reference implementation of Register Algebra, an exact integer
  and rational arithmetic in which an integer N is represented as a pair of
  integer registers (a, b) with N = 2a + 3b, and a rational is kept as an
  unevaluated image of division. Includes a script reproducing the empirical
  evaluation reported in the accompanying article.
keywords:
  - exact arithmetic
  - rational arithmetic
  - computer algebra
  - number representation
  - field of fractions
  - reproducible research
